BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (Lender capacity kills deals that look fundable on paper. Sua Truong placed seven Subway franchises for one client at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (TD, then watched the bank refuse the eighth. The portfolio was full of Subways, and the concentration had become) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (high risk. Truong is blunt that the underwriters understood the business fine; the bank simply could not hold any more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (of it in the portfolio [cqOh0arlXGU @ 00:03:46]. Truong also points out that declines work differently in the two) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (worlds. On the residential side, once an underwriter declines a file it cannot be resubmitted. A commercial deal can go) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (back in after restructuring, so a commercial decline is a prompt to fix the structure rather than a dead file) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm ([cqOh0arlXGU @ 00:10:06]. Bill Rapp names the cost of having no alternative when one lender says no: lost) Tj ET
