BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 544.10 Tm (on the equipment, 'lenders definitely do not want to take a second position on an asset,' and only real estate with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 528.87 Tm (significant equity behaves differently [WfAvAf4wk0k @ 00:04:07]. The structural trap is MCA money for equipment.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 513.65 Tm (Christopher pitched a $25,000 to $30,000 revenue company buying at auction with a cash advance, and Ryan shut it) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 498.42 Tm (down: repayment hits daily or weekly, the client is 'bleeding money,' can default and lose the equipment, and no lender) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 483.20 Tm (waits six months for a farmer's harvest; 'that's not how a cash advance works' [jq-MYGn7i3I @ 00:11:56]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 467.97 Tm (cheapest failure to avoid is the first one: ask outright whether the client is buying equipment or borrowing against) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 452.75 Tm (existing equipment, because skipping that question sends the file down a 'rabbit hole' [DSEdy5KFvBs @ 00:01:45].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 437.52 Tm (Recent model years, VINs on vehicles and a resale test on every asset line screen out dead files early.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 422.30 Tm (Equipment Finance Academy lists six beginner mistakes that kill pipelines: serving every industry, sending incomplete) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 407.07 Tm (applications, promising approval, skipping follow-up, chasing leads over referral relationships, and leaning on a single) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 391.85 Tm (course or lender [nN3wD1zIjqM @ 00:08:33]. The incomplete-package problem is mechanical: a lender-ready file with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 376.62 Tm (legal business name, owner info, time in business, equipment, vendor, exact cost and signed credit authorization can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 361.40 Tm (decided in four hours, while anything short lands in the 'more information needed' pile, because 'lenders do not fund) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 346.17 Tm (conversations' [dc0_7D431kI @ 00:03:50]. Josh Feinberg's numbers show what quitting early costs: bought leads close) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 330.95 Tm (at 1.5 to 2% in the first two months but climb to 6 to 7% by month 12 through follow-up, and Matty adds that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 315.72 Tm (one-to-three-month mindset buys one to three months of longevity, while an ex-roommate still closes deals a year out) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 300.50 Tm (by calling every 60 days [Oq4y-D6sylo @ 00:09:14]. The application itself leaks too: Josh and Matty put live phone) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 285.27 Tm (applications at about 50% completion versus roughly 20% by email, and on MCA files they stay on the call until bank) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 270.05 Tm (statements arrive [Oq4y-D6sylo @ 00:44:42]. Log every stalled file with source, equipment, missing documents, lender) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 254.82 Tm (and stall point.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 239.60 Tm (Run the unit math before buying anything. Equipment Finance Academy's own example states '$50,000 at 5%' as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 224.37 Tm ('$2,550' and then works it as $2,500; its Path A of bought leads nets about $1,700 after 20 hours, while Path B, one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 209.15 Tm (page producing three inbound leads, two packages and one funding, keeps $2,500 at zero lead cost [dc0_7D431kI @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 193.92 Tm (00:05:37]. Josh Feinberg's exclusive program runs $50 a lead with a 30-lead monthly floor and a three-month) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 178.70 Tm (commitment, so a broker is in for $4,500 before going month-to-month, against a reported one to two deals per 30 leads) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 163.47 Tm ([Oq4y-D6sylo @ 00:21:25]. Commission timing carries its own reversal risk: Jermaine is cut a check the moment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 148.25 Tm (paperwork is signed, but clawbacks trigger on a first-payment default or inside 90 days, a hit Jermaine has taken twice) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 133.02 Tm (across roughly 1,500 deals [L2-ax8GoKVw @ 00:24:08]. Cheryl Tibbs says new brokers quit because nobody handed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 117.80 Tm (them lender contacts, approvable deal structuring, or an answer to the vendor question 'Why should I send you my) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 102.57 Tm (deals?', and that the learning curve cost Tibbs years, money and sleep, which most people never survive) Tj ET
