BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Detail: McMahon sets up a conference call with an underwriter, routes to a factor, MCA, PO funder or equipment) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (lessor, and the broker collects 10-15% of the monthly fee [Simon White \(SEO, AEO & Digital & Marketing\) -) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (G9RrpSanefM @ 00:22:49]) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (Evan Wagner walks a full borrowing base through his Michael Scott Paper Co. example. AR more than 30 days past) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (due is ineligible and strips 9% of the pool, then a concentration cap removes about 11% more, since most lenders) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (implement a 25% concentration threshold [oobK7A-p9-U @ 00:33:19]. Net eligible AR of 586 at an 85-cent advance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (yields 498. Finished goods advance at the lesser of 65 cents or 85% of NOLV, raw materials up to about 50%, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (work in process and packaging get nothing; inventory sitting at small locations like Nashua and Utica is ineligible. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (base totals $832K against a $1M cap, less a $42K AP reserve, for $790K, leaving $162K of excess availability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm ([oobK7A-p9-U @ 00:45:24]. Financely Group states the same formula in one line: eligible receivables plus inventory,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm (times advance rates, minus reserves, with net availability the lesser of the base or total commitments, and inventory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (must be saleable and unencumbered [xY3rD_awSEg @ 00:00:40]. FinanceKid quotes the inventory advance as usually) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (80% of net orderly liquidation value, below market value, and pairs it with invoice factoring [u5hujmtiiaY @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (00:13:38]. Wagner then measures liquidity as excess availability plus cash against burn: most lenders want twelve) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (months of historical burn covered, and three months is a tough call.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (Pricing is quoted openly. FinanceKid prices recourse factoring at up to 90% of eligible receivables aged 90 days or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (less: on $1,000 of invoices, $900 is advanced, a 5% fee costs $45, and $55 comes back after 20 days. Non-recourse) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (drops to 70 to 80% with higher fees, so the same $1,000 advances $700, carries a $105 fee at 15%, and rebates $195) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm ([u5hujmtiiaY @ 00:04:44]. Purchase order advances hinge on the customer, not the borrower: 90% for a safe customer,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (70 to 80% for a riskier one, with a 7% fee in the worked example [u5hujmtiiaY @ 00:08:59]. Bob McMahon of Aegis) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (Factors puts typical factoring near 2.5% per 30 days and frames 3% on $100K, or $3,000, as comparable to the $2,000) Tj ET
