BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 381.77 Tm (Firsthand Failure Modes, Traps & Economics Checks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 359.55 Tm (The borrowing base is where deal sizes collapse, and the haircut math is firsthand. Financely Group warns that lenders) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 344.32 Tm (underwrite collectibility, not face value, tracking aging, dilution, and cross-aging [xY3rD_awSEg @ 00:01:08]. Evan) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 329.10 Tm (Wagner walks the Michael Scott Paper Co. book through the knife: AR more than 30 days past due is ineligible,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.87 Tm (stripping 9%, and a concentration cap, where most lenders implement a 25% threshold, strips about 11% more) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 298.65 Tm ([oobK7A-p9-U @ 00:33:19]. Net eligible AR of 586 advanced at 85 cents yields 498. Inventory gets cut harder:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 283.42 Tm (finished goods advance at the lesser of 65 cents or 85% of NOLV, raw materials up to about 50%, WIP and packaging) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 268.20 Tm (are excluded, and stock sitting at small locations like Nashua and Utica is ineligible. Stack it up and a $1M facility) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.97 Tm (shows a borrowing base of $832K, less a $42K AP reserve, for $790K available and only $162K of excess availability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.75 Tm ([oobK7A-p9-U @ 00:45:24]. Wagner's reason is blunt: asset-based lenders are underwriting to a liquidation, to a worst) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 222.52 Tm (case scenario [oobK7A-p9-U @ 00:34:49]. The economics check follows from Financely's formula that net availability) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 207.30 Tm (is the lesser of the borrowing base or total commitments: model eligible collateral after aging, concentration, location,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 192.07 Tm (and reserve cuts before promising a client any number.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 176.85 Tm (Inventory-heavy and burn-heavy borrowers are the second trap. FinanceKid says many people call inventory financing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 161.62 Tm (the last alternative among ABL options because of the double fees [u5hujmtiiaY @ 00:16:25]. The stack he lists:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 146.40 Tm (Prime+4-6%, plus warehousing costs, audits every 3-6 months, and a high DIO that is risky and can lead to default) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 131.17 Tm ([u5hujmtiiaY @ 00:18:04]. The positive case he allows is narrow: building stock in June for December demand.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 115.95 Tm (Wagner adds the liquidity test lenders actually run: excess availability plus cash, measured against burn, where three) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 100.72 Tm (months of coverage is a tough call and most lenders prefer enough liquidity to cover at least 12 months of historical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 85.50 Tm (burn [oobK7A-p9-U @ 00:48:23]. He also flags that later-stage equity investors resist using their dollars to buy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 70.27 Tm (inventory, which is why the paper company leaned on roughly $628,000 of ABL after Staples slowed to 45 days and) Tj ET
