BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 693.77 Tm (Every practitioner who works MCA files describes the same trap door. Once the advance funds, the funder files a UCC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 678.55 Tm (filing. Sebastian Boore of The Approved Guy says that filing makes it very difficult to get a better product, so the only) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 663.32 Tm (offer left is another advance. He has seen up to seven positions stacked against one business [8x-cfQhQpPU @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 648.10 Tm (00:01:03]. Meredith at Berkshire Financial Services calls it a blanket lien over equipment, inventory, bank accounts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 632.87 Tm (and especially future receivables. That lien blocks new financing, lets funders freeze accounts, and gives them a pretext) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 617.65 Tm (to contact customers and reroute payments [V8S0sywozwU @ 00:00:15]. Mick Wadley of Gap Funding maps the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 602.42 Tm (spiral step by step. The first advance covers payroll, a repair or an equipment purchase. The daily pull eats more cash) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 587.20 Tm (than expected, so a second advance covers the gap the first one created, and then a third follows. Once combined) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 571.97 Tm (withdrawals hit thirty to forty percent of daily card receipts, most businesses cannot cover rent, payroll and inventory) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 556.75 Tm ([OWlnOeMGBkg @ 00:01:18]. The Parkins & Rubio attorneys define stacking as using a new MCA to pay off an old) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 541.52 Tm (one. They read it as a sign of a repeated cash flow problem, not a short-term hiccup. They add that stacking is a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 526.30 Tm (refinancing fact that pushes a court toward treating the deal as a loan [A8iNT8Ctrhk @ 00:07:10].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 511.07 Tm (The speakers also agree on how the product gets sold. Boore says boiler-room brokers and direct lenders market all day) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 495.85 Tm (to businesses that have good credit and no business taking an MCA. The pitch is that there is no interest rate, just a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 480.62 Tm (factor rate of 1.35 or 1.45, sometimes 1.25. The advance is 80 to 90 percent of the average monthly statement, repaid) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 465.40 Tm (by daily or weekly debits over three to twelve months [8x-cfQhQpPU @ 00:01:25]. Zach Siegel of Small Biz Heroes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 450.17 Tm (adds that most brokers blowing up the phone sell only that one product, and many hold no license. Their standard hook) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 434.95 Tm (is: make payments for a month or two and you will qualify for a line of credit. That line rarely shows up. The broker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 419.72 Tm (ghosts or offers one more short-term position [w-ETPb-Trek @ 00:01:36]. David Rutz, founder of David Allen Capital,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 404.50 Tm (told his ISO force about a construction client whose prior broker placed four advances on the same day for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 389.27 Tm (commission. None of the four lenders was told about the others. The client was left sending 40 percent of sales to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 374.05 Tm (payments, about 80,000 a month out of 200,000 in revenue [i0yXJe_x34I @ 00:26:34]. Zoryn Capital's operator states) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 358.82 Tm (one rule that separates winners from casualties. The advance has to be profit-based: take it only if it makes you money,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 343.60 Tm (and never to pay bills or survive [ORF9Ue9ge8A @ 00:06:23].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 328.37 Tm (Before any exit, the agreed first move is to stop adding positions. Siegel's rule: if you carry more than three MCAs,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (take no new ones while the fix is underway, because every new position makes the business harder to save. From that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (point the goal is fewer, cheaper and slower payments, not shorter, faster and more expensive ones [w-ETPb-Trek @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 282.70 Tm (00:03:16]. The practitioners rank the exits in the same order. Boore lists an SBA 7\(a\), a business term loan or a line of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 267.47 Tm (credit for owners who have good credit and time. Everyone else gets an attorney-led MCA restructure [dDwHOnFlzaA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 252.25 Tm (@ 00:01:08]. Michael Granados calls refinance or consolidation into a new loan the fastest route. It takes 10 to 15 days,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 237.02 Tm (and up to 30 days of underwriting when a bank is involved. It only works if the owner clears the credit score and debt) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 221.80 Tm (service coverage hurdles; otherwise he pushes restructuring [lBvWGt7bnCw @ 00:00:14]. Wadley's matrix lands in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 206.57 Tm (same place. If revenue is solid and the problem is payment structure, roll the balances into a term loan, HELOC, line of) Tj ET
