BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (personal income counts for zero, tax returns showing big depreciation and cost-segregation losses are great at tax time) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (and terrible at bank time, and the DSCR loan removes that bottleneck so each new deal makes the next one easier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (instead of piling onto a debt-to-income ratio [-W2ThDxeu-o @ 00:05:36]. Andrew Russell watched a Brooklyn client) Tj ET
